  "technical_internal_limitation": "The decisive feasibility check is not the scalar identity \\(u v+(1/4-u^2)t=0\\), which holds cellwise. It is whether smooth full-density gluing and posterior-sign coupling preserve the cost \\(D_H\\lesssim n t^{a_0}\\). If every valid finite paired-cell coupling instead costs order \\(n h^d t\\), then the \\(q\\)-private term must be removed and the matched theorem collapses to the \\(\\gamma\\)-private-regression or a separately derived private-Gram branch.",
